From: Pear contributors
Subject: [PATCH] wine: advertise the selected native-only Darwin architecture

Base: Wine 4e819f054dd2d9ee855ee3f1e30d8c1bb8f80fcf plus preceding Pear patches
through 0003k. Original Pear configuration and architecture-policy correction.
A Darwin ARM64 build with only aarch64 PE modules has no runnable I386/AMD64
companion. The upstream server nevertheless advertises those architectures,
causing real Wineboot initialization to start an absent syswow64/rundll32.exe.
Derive an explicit server policy from the host and selected PE targets. Keep
all upstream non-Darwin, other-host, companion-target and 32-bit-prefix paths
unchanged. Consumers receive the corrected server capability list; no Wineboot
initialization, failed exit, or fixture observation is bypassed. Generated
configure changes match configure.ac without unrelated regeneration. Existing
LGPL-2.1-or-later notices are preserved and apply. This change does not qualify
translated execution, ARM64EC or game support.

